{"name":"Egyptian Nile","hex":"#70775c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Nile","blocks":[{"text":"The Nile is a major north-flowing river in northeast Africa which empties into the Mediterranean Sea. At 7,088 kilometers (4,404 mi) long, it is the longest river in the world, although the volume of water it carries is much smaller than other major rivers such as the Amazon or the Congo. The Nile has played a central role in the environmental, economic, and cultural history of Africa for millennia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Beautiful_nature_along_Nile_River_01.jpg/330px-Beautiful_nature_along_Nile_River_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nile","wikidata":"Q3392"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Whiteandblueniles.jpg/500px-Whiteandblueniles.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Whiteandblueniles.jpg/500px-Whiteandblueniles.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The distinct colors of the White Nile (left) and the Blue Nile (right) are visible where they merge to form the main Nile (top left).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWhiteandblueniles.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Assuan-Hochdamm_15.JPG/500px-Assuan-Hochdamm_15.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Assuan-Hochdamm_15.JPG/1280px-Assuan-Hochdamm_15.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Assuan-Hochdamm_15.JPG/500px-Assuan-Hochdamm_15.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"T